<section aria-labelledby="where-heading" class="px-4 py-14 sm:px-6 sm:py-16 lg:px-8">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-4xl text-center" data-reveal-group>
    <h2 id="where-heading" data-reveal class="text-3xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-text sm:text-4xl">
      Security that runs where you build, inside your coding agent.
    </h2>
    <p data-reveal class="mt-6 text-lg leading-relaxed text-text-muted">
      LyraShield runs as an MCP server in Cursor, Claude Code, VS Code + GitHub Copilot, Windsurf, Codex, OpenCode, and other compatible clients. Your agent can read findings, check launch readiness, start a targeted review, and draft the release record without you switching tools. Anything that would change code or publish a report requires your explicit approval on the controlling terminal and fails closed when no terminal is present. You are not adding another dashboard to check. You are giving the agent that wrote the code the loop to review it.
    </p>
    <div class="mt-10 flex flex-wrap items-center justify-center gap-3" data-reveal-group>
      <span data-reveal="scale" class="lift rounded-full border border-border bg-bg-raised px-4 py-2 text-sm text-text-muted hover:border-accent hover:text-text">VS Code + GitHub Copilot</span>
      <span data-reveal="scale" class="lift rounded-full border border-border bg-bg-raised px-4 py-2 text-sm text-text-muted hover:border-accent hover:text-text">Claude Code</span>
      <span data-reveal="scale" class="lift rounded-full border border-border bg-bg-raised px-4 py-2 text-sm text-text-muted hover:border-accent hover:text-text">Windsurf</span>
      <span data-reveal="scale" class="lift rounded-full border border-border bg-bg-raised px-4 py-2 text-sm text-text-muted hover:border-accent hover:text-text">Codex</span>
      <span data-reveal="scale" class="lift rounded-full border border-border bg-bg-raised px-4 py-2 text-sm text-text-muted hover:border-accent hover:text-text">OpenCode</span>
      <span data-reveal="scale" class="lift rounded-full border border-border bg-bg-raised px-4 py-2 text-sm text-text-muted hover:border-accent hover:text-text">Any compatible MCP client</span>
    </div>
    <p data-reveal class="mt-6 text-sm text-text-muted">
      Setup is one command: <code class="rounded bg-bg-raised px-1.5 py-0.5 font-mono text-[0.8em] text-text">npx lyrashield init</code> detects your client and writes the config. See the <a href="/docs/integrations" class="font-semibold text-accent underline decoration-accent/40 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-accent">per-agent setup guides</a>.
    </p>
  </div>

  {/* What the loop looks like from inside a coding agent. The transcript is real
      text, not an image, so it stays crawlable and screen-reader readable; only
      the window chrome and the caret are decorative. */}
  <figure class="mcp-term mx-auto mt-12 max-w-3xl" data-reveal="scale">
    <div class="mcp-term__chrome" aria-hidden="true">
      <span></span><span></span><span></span>
      <p>your coding agent — LyraShield MCP</p>
    </div>
    <pre class="mcp-term__body"><code><span class="mcp-term__you">you</span>  check this app before I ship it
<span class="mcp-term__sys">lyrashield</span>  scope confirmed · authorized target only
<span class="mcp-term__sys">lyrashield</span>  review running · layers kept separate
<span class="mcp-term__sys">lyrashield</span>  4 detected · 2 independently verified · 1 inconclusive
<span class="mcp-term__you">you</span>  fix the verified one
<span class="mcp-term__sys">lyrashield</span>  fix proposal staged · plain-English explanation + patch
<span class="mcp-term__warn">      ⚠ approval required on this terminal · nothing auto-merges</span>
<span class="mcp-term__warn">      approve? [y/N]</span><span class="mcp-term__caret" aria-hidden="true"></span></code></pre>
    <figcaption class="mcp-term__caption">
      Illustrative session. The approval gate is real: a fix proposal cannot execute unless a
      server-generated patch is bound to your explicit approval on the controlling terminal, and it
      fails closed when no terminal is present.
    </figcaption>
  </figure>
</section>

